QuestGuidance.Register("en",236,{
[7521]="70039C13\n1\tTravel to Fenmarch\tThane Sparhafoc is at Fenmarch, east of the lumber-yard. Guthláf stayed behind to assist in the cleaning efforts at the lumber yard, but asked to have a message relayed to his father, Thane Sparhafoc.\n2\tTalk to Thane Sparhafoc\tThane Sparhafoc is in the Mead Hall, in the eastern part of Fenmarch. Guthláf asked you to inform his father, Thane Sparhafoc, about the troubles at the lumber-yard.\n",
[7522]="7006A1DD\n1\tDefeat Azagath's Sea-Shadow and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Azagath's crew and pursue the Kindred through the fallen temple.\n2\tDefeat Belondor and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Belondor and his crew to pursue Azagath through the fallen temple.\n3\tDefeat Umshûra the Glutton\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Umshûra the Glutton.\n4\tCompleted: Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 1\tAzagath Sea-shadow and Nakâsi Wave-reaper are missing. Belondor returns to Umbar Baharbêl in disgrace and you defeated Umshûra the Glutton, a foul denizen of the deep. You have completed Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 1. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Monday, Thursday, and Saturday.\n",
[7523]="7006A1DB\n1\tDefeat Azagath's Sea-Shadow and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Azagath's crew and pursue the Kindred through the fallen temple.\n2\tDefeat Belondor and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Belondor and his crew to pursue Azagath through the fallen temple.\n3\tDefeat Umshûra the Glutton\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Umshûra the Glutton.\n4\tCompleted: Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 2\tAzagath Sea-shadow and Nakâsi Wave-reaper are missing. Belondor returns to Umbar Baharbêl in disgrace and you defeated Umshûra the Glutton, a foul denizen of the deep. You have completed Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 2. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Thursday.\n",
[7524]="7006A1DC\n1\tDefeat Azagath's Sea-Shadow and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Azagath's crew and pursue the Kindred through the fallen temple.\n2\tDefeat Belondor and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Belondor and his crew to pursue Azagath through the fallen temple.\n3\tDefeat Umshûra the Glutton\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Umshûra the Glutton.\n4\tCompleted: Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 3\tAzagath Sea-shadow and Nakâsi Wave-reaper are missing. Belondor returns to Umbar Baharbêl in disgrace and you defeated Umshûra the Glutton, a foul denizen of the deep. You have completed Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 3. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Thursday.\n",
[7525]="7006A1DA\n1\tDefeat Azagath's Sea-Shadow and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Azagath's crew and pursue the Kindred through the fallen temple.\n2\tDefeat Belondor and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Belondor and his crew to pursue Azagath through the fallen temple.\n3\tDefeat Umshûra the Glutton\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Umshûra the Glutton.\n4\tCompleted: Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 4\tAzagath Sea-shadow and Nakâsi Wave-reaper are missing. Belondor returns to Umbar Baharbêl in disgrace and you defeated Umshûra the Glutton, a foul denizen of the deep. You have completed Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 4. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Thursday.\n",
[7526]="7006A1D9\n1\tDefeat Azagath's Sea-Shadow and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Azagath's crew and pursue the Kindred through the fallen temple.\n2\tDefeat Belondor and his crew\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Belondor and his crew to pursue Azagath through the fallen temple.\n3\tDefeat Umshûra the Glutton\tAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred. Defeat Umshûra the Glutton.\n4\tCompleted: Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 5\tAzagath Sea-shadow and Nakâsi Wave-reaper are missing. Belondor returns to Umbar Baharbêl in disgrace and you defeated Umshûra the Glutton, a foul denizen of the deep. You have completed Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 5. NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Thursday.\n",
[7527]="7002BD4E\n1\tDefeat Ironarm\tDefeat the abominations in Saruman's laboratories in the pits of Isengard, particularly the troll Ironarm.\n",
[7528]="70071B7E\n1\tMeet Mêshaget at the entrance to Lâkindar\tMêshaget promised to explain what is going on when you meet at the top of the great staircase at Lâkindar's entrance. Lâkindar is located far to the south of Jiret-menêsh in An Shêru.\n2\tTalk to Mêshaget outside of Lâkindar\tYou have travelled to Lâkindar and found Mêshaget waiting for you. You should talk to him.\n3\tEnter the Quelling-house\tMêshaget wants to ensure neither of you were followed here. You should enter the Quelling-house and assess the situation.\n4\tDefeat wights (total: 8)\tThe dead have awoken and are roaming the halls of Lâkindar. You should defeat some of the wights to clear the way for Mêshaget.\n5\tFind the entrance to the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding\tYou have cleared a path in the Quelling-house and have yet to see Mêshaget. You should search for the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding.\n6\tComplete Instance: Into the Quelling-house\tAs you approached what you thought was the entrance to the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding, you heard a frightened scream from inside. It must be Mêshaget! You should enter the tomb and help him.\n7\tTalk to Châmelek Gêta\tFollowing a confrontation with Sâdikiz the Sky-hungry and his Ordâkhai allies, you have helped an injured Mêshaget return to Jiret-menêsh where you were both immediately brought before an angry Châmelek Gêta.\n8\tTalk to Mêshaget\tChâmelek Gêta is at once furious with you both but also awestruck at having the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding handed to her. She demands Mêshaget explain what this is about. You should talk to Mêshaget.\n9\tTalk to Châmelek Gêta\tMêshaget has pleaded his case with Châmelek Gêta as well as he could, asking only that she take the time to review the journal and consider the option of making alliances and fortifying the city. You should talk to Châmelek Gêta to hear her response.\n10\tTalk to Mêshaget\tChâmelek Gêta agreed to examine the plans in the journal and discuss the situation with Mêshaget after she has done so. You should talk to Mêshaget inside the Gêta's hall.\n",
[7529]="7000173C\n1\tTalk to Chief Tuokki\tThe Earth-kin chief is in his village on the west side of the Ram Dúath. Arohir has sent you to the Earth-kin of the Ram Dúath to offer aid against the forces of Angmar that are harrying them.\n",
[7530]="7000BFC3\n1\tTalk to Glorfindel\tGlorfindel is near the Bruinen in Rivendell. Faimir suggests that you speak with Glorfindel and learn what it is that troubles him.\n2\tTalk to Iorelen\tIorelen is at Iorelen's camp far to the north-east in Angmar. Glorfindel requested that you seek Iorelen and learn whether he still lives.\n",
[7531]="7001752D\n1\tHelp Ymar rid the Dark Delvings of the glowing worms\030Help Moggi rid the Dark Delvings of the terrible things in the dark\030Recover the runes from the Dark Delvings for Pentlenn\030Discover the secret of the Dark Delvings for Glorelloth\tComplete the task set before you by Ymar, Moggi, Pentlenn and Glorelloth surrounding the Dark Delvings and then return to Gelirwen. Gelirwen wishes to know what secrets the darkest halls of Moria can offer the expedition to the Shadowed Refuge.\n2\tTalk to Gelirwen at the Shadowed Refuge\tGelirwen is at the Shadowed Refuge. You completed all tasks set before you by Moggi, Ymar, Glorelloth, and Pentlenn and should return to Gelirwen with this news.\n",
[7532]="7005465B\n1\tTalk to Felgúr\tFelgúr has continued ahead to Torech Ungol, and is waiting at the top of the Winding Stair. You should climb the Winding Stair and find Felgúr.\n2\tComplete 'Instance: She Who Walks in the Darkness'\tFelgúr has tracked his people to the top of the Winding Stair. You should talk to Felgúr, and be ready for a fight.\n3\tTalk to Celeborn\030Talk to Legolas\tCeleborn and Legolas are outside Torech Ungol, at the top of the Winding Stair. You should talk to Celeborn and Legolas.\n4\tHelp Celeborn with 'Re-forming the Snare'\030Help Celeborn with 'Caging the Spiders'\tCeleborn has asked for your help containing the spiders in Torech Ungol. You should help Celeborn with 'Re-forming the Snare' and 'Caging the Spiders'.\n5\tTalk to Celeborn\tCeleborn can be found outside Torech Ungol. You should talk to Celeborn.\n6\tTalk to Mablung\tCeleborn has asked you to swiftly return to the rangers in Echad Taerdrim. You should return to the rangers and talk to Mablung. Speak to Legolas to return there quickly.\n",
[7533]="70059739\n1\tTalk to the angry tree\tThe angry tree can be found on the road in the northern Wildwood. Talk to the angry tree.\n",
[7534]="700005BE\n1\tTalk to Walt Whitrose in Nen Harn\tWalt Whitrose is camped within the ruins at the the western edge of the lake known as Nen Harn. Gil Sandheaver asked you to speak with Walt Whitrose about the strange thing he saw north of the Far Chetwood.\n",
[7535]="70040AFE\n1\tSearch for the missing workers\tThe workers can be found in the forest south of Tadrent, in the foothills of the Emyn Ernil, above the beacon Nendath. You should find the workers there and help them finish their task.\n2\tCollect wood (total: 5)\030Examine one of the bodies\tThe workers' camp-site can be found in the forest south of Tadrent, in the foothills of the Emyn Ernil, above the beacon Nendath. You should examine a body and collect wood for Haelam.\n3\tBring the wood back to Haelam in Tadrent\tHaelam is located in the village of Tadrent. Bring the wood back to Haelam in the village of Tadrent.\n4\tBuild crate (total: 2)\tThe workbench is located near Haelam in Tadrent. Use the workbench to build crates for Haelam.\n5\tSpeak with Haelam\tHaelam is located in the village of Tadrent. Speak with Haelam.\n",
[7536]="70068245\n1\tFollow the trail of footprints out of Kafagur\tShúkurz has left behind a trail of footprints leading out of the northern side of Kafagur. You should follow it.\n2\tTalk to Phocas\tYou have found Shúkurz and Phocas outside Kafagur, near the northern side. You should talk to Phocas.\n3\tTalk to Shúkurz\tYou have found Shúkurz and Phocas outside Kafagur, near the northern side. You should talk to Shúkurz.\n4\tTalk to Shúkurz in Kafagur\tShúkurz has asked you to talk to him back in Kafagur.\n",
[7537]="70019506\n1\tUse your Battle Shout on the training-dummy, then strike it with your skill Devastating Blow\tUse Devastating Blowon the training-dummy nearby. HINT: Captains rely on their Battle Shout to put them into a Battle-Readied State. While in this state, Captains can use special skills such as Devastating Blow, an effective attack that deals a great deal of damage. Attack the Training Dummy with your Battle Shout to put you into a Battle-Readied State and then attack the dummy with your Devastating Blow.\n2\tTalk to the Captain Trainer in Archet\tThe Captain Trainer is in the training grounds of Archet, very near the gate. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7538]="70018F4E\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Shield Swipe\tSpeak with the trainer again and learn the skill Shield Swipe. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Guardian Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel, or double-click the skill, and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Guardians rely on Reactive Skills to deal damage and generate Threat against their enemies. Shield Swipe requires that the Guardian Block an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill. Head over to the Training-Dummies to the north of the trainer and attack it until you successfully block one of their attacks. If you're having trouble getting a block, try using Guardian's Ward to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks. Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your Shield Swipe skill. Strike the Targeting Dummy with Shield Swipe.\n2\tTalk to the Guardian Trainer in Edhelion\tNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n3\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion. You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.\n",
[7539]="7001939A\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Shield Swipe\tYou should speak with the trainer again and learn the skill Shield Swipe. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Guardian Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel -- or double-click the skill -- and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Guardians rely on Reactive Skills to deal damage and generate Threat against their enemies. Shield Swipe requires that the Guardian Block an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill. Head over to the Training-Dummies to the north of the trainer and attack it until you successfully block one of their attacks. If you're having trouble getting a block, try using Guardian's Ward to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks. Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your Shield Swipe skill. Strike the Targeting Dummy with Shield Swipe.\n2\tTalk to the Guardian Trainer at Frerin's Court\tThe Guardian Trainer is in Frerin's Court. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7540]="70018F4F\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Penetrating Shot\tSpeak with the trainer again and learn the skill Penetrating Shot. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Hunter Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel, or double-click the skill, and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: (Hunters need Focus to use some of their special shots, and Penetrating Shot is such a skill. Use your Quick Shot ability until you have 3 Focus points, then use Penetrating Shot.\n2\tTalk to the Hunter Trainer in Edhelion\tNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n3\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion. You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.\n",
[7541]="700467A8\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Penetrating Shot\tYou should speak with the trainer again and learn the skill Penetrating Shot. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Hunter Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel -- or double-click the skill -- and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Hunters need Focus to use some of their special shots, and Penetrating Shot is such a skill. Use your Quick Shot ability until you have 3 Focus points, then use Penetrating Shot.\n2\tTalk to the Hunter Trainer at Frerin's Court\tThe Hunter Trainer is in Frerin's Court. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7542]="70018F50\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Burning Embers.\tYou should speak with the trainer again and learn the skill Burning Embers. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Lore-master Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel -- or double-click the skill -- and you will successfully purchase the skill.\n2\tTalk to the Lore-master Trainer in Edhelion\tNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n3\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion. You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.\n",
[7543]="70019507\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Burning Embers\tUse the skill Burning Embers on the training-dummy nearby.\n2\tTalk to the Lore-master Trainer at Archet\tThe Lore-master Trainer is in Archet, west of the training grounds. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7544]="70019398\n1\tUse the skill Ballad of Swiftness on the training-dummy\tYou should speak with the trainer again and learn the skill Major Ballad. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Minstrel Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel -- or double-click the skill -- and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Minstrels use Ballads to attack their enemies and empower themselves. These skills operate on a rotating system that allows the minstrel to have three special buffs on themselves at any time. After the third buff is applied the next Ballad played will overwrite the first, then the second and so on.\n2\tTalk to the Minstrel Trainer at Frerin's Court\tThe Minstrel Trainer is in Frerin's Court. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7545]="70018F51\n1\tUse the skill Major Ballad on the training-dummy\tSpeak with the trainer again and learn the skill Major Ballad. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. HINT: Minstrels use Ballads to attack their enemies and empower themselves. These skills operate on a rotating system that allows the minstrel to have three special buffs on themselves at any time. After the third buff is applied the next Ballad played will overwrite the first, then the second and so on.\n2\tTalk to the Minstrel Trainer in Edhelion\tNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n3\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion. You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.\n",
[7546]="700248C2\n1\tExamine patches of strange soil along the river (total: 4)\030Collect samples from sick bears (total: 4)\tThe dwarves of Dwalin's party came over the fields to the west of Frerin's Court when they arrived. You should begin your search by following the road west to see if there is any evidence for the source of the plague that afflicts the dwarves.\n2\tTell Dwalin about the source of the dwarves' sickness\tDwalin awaits word in Frerin's Court, east of the river where you examined the soil. You should speak with Dwalin in Frerin's Court and let him know that the river itself seems poisoned by some sickly rot.\n",
[7547]="70022A6A\n1\tGo to Combe to plead for aid against the Blackwold threat\tThe Combe Gate is not far to the west of Sprigley's Farm, along the road south from the town of Archet. You should ask for assistance in Combe, for they have many well-equipped soldiers there due to their proximity to the dangerous Chetwood.\n2\tReturn to Cal Sprigley with your dire news\tCal Sprigley is at his farm in the southernmost tip of Archet. You should return to Cal and inform him that the road to Combe is blocked at the gate, and Archet will be on its own.\n3\tBring Sprigley's letter of warning to Brackenbrook\tCaptain Brackenbrook is within the walls of the town of Archet. You should return to Brackenbrook with Cal Sprigley's letter as proof of the Blackwolds' intentions. He must be told that the southern part of Archet is rife with signs of an impending raid.\n",
[7548]="700248D5\n1\tDefeat guards of the mountain path (total: 4)\030Explore the mountainside for the source of the poison\tThe mountain-path is north-west of Frerin's Court in Ered Luin. You should climb the mountain path and find the source of the befouled waters and fend off any guards of the corruption along the way.\n2\tTalk to Elrohir, the brother of Elladan\tElrohir of Rivendell, the other son of Elrond, stands outside the entrance to a cave on the mountain path. You should speak with Elrohir of your errand for Dwalin and Elladan.\n",
[7549]="70018F52\n1\tUse the skill Shocking Words on the training-dummy\tSpeak with the trainer again and learn the skill Shocking Words. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Rune-keeper Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel, or double-click the skill, and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Runekeepers require Battle Attunement to use offensive skills, and Healing Attunement to cast healing spells. Attunement is raised or lowered through the use of similar skills. Offensive Skills typically have Red backgrounds, and Healing skills typically have Green backgrounds. Use your offensive skills to raise your Battle Attunement to three and then use your Shocking Words skill.\n2\tTalk to the Rune-keeperTrainer in Edhelion\tNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n3\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion. You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.\n",
[7550]="70019397\n1\tUse the skill Shocking Words on the training-dummy\tYou should speak with the trainer again and learn the skill Shocking Words. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Rune-keeper Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel -- or double-click the skill -- and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Runekeepers require Battle Attunement to use offensive skills, and Healing Attunement to cast healing spells. Attunement is raised or lowered through the use of similar skills. Offensive Skills typically have Red backgrounds, and Healing skills typically have Green backgrounds. Use your offensive skills to raise your Battle Attunement to three and then use your Shocking Words skill.\n2\tTalk to the Rune-keeperTrainer in Frerin's Court\tThe Rune-keeper Trainer is in Frerin's Court. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7551]="70022A8F\n1\tTalk to Atli Spider-bane about the Old East Path\tAtli Spider-bane stands outside the Hunter's Lodge. You should speak with Atli Spider-bane and learn what you can about the Old East Path.\n2\tDefeat spiders on the Old East Path (total: 4)\030See if the wall is still intact\tThe Old East Path cuts into the large hill west of the Hunting Lodge. You should explore the Old East Path to see how it can be used to get an advantage over the Blackwolds when they attack.\n3\tReturn to Jon Brackenbrook with the hopeful news\tJon Brackenbrook is at the Hunter's Lodge in the north-east corner of Archet. You should tell Jon Brackenbrook of the dead end and the slaughtered Blackwold scout at the end of the Old East Path.\n",
[7552]="70019505\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with 'Shield-swipe'\tUse your Shield-swipe skill on the Training-dummy nearby. HINT: Guardians rely on Reactive Skills to deal damage and generate Threat against their enemies. Shield-swipe requires that the Guardian Block an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill. Head over to the Training-dummies to the north and attack one until you successfully block one of its attacks. If you're having trouble getting a block, try using Guardian's Ward to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks. Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your Shield-swipe skill. Strike the Training-dummy with Shield-swipe.\n2\tTalk to the Guardian Trainer in Archet\tThe Guardian Trainer is in the training ground in Archet. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n",
})
